A ((software)) package by ((Richard Curnow)) which parses and glosses Lojban text into English.

[http://www.rrbcurnow.freeuk.com/jbofihe/]

''An online version is available at [http://www.lojban.org/jboski] --pne''

It also provides utilities for the classification of words, and the construction of lujvo.

The name arose due to a lack of creativity on my part when I made the first release.  I just took the name ''Babelfish'' (the famous translation engine
on Altavista) and adapted it a bit to give ''Lojbanic fish''.  So originally I guess it links back to ''The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy'' by Douglas Adams, but with rather a lot of obscure adaption.  ''mi'e ((Richard Curnow|ritcrd.))''
